# Claude Code local session state — not part of the marketplace
.claude/*
# ...except this repo's own mirrors of the skills it ships, which are versioned with
# the repo so they cannot silently drift from the plugin skills they mirror.
#
# The whole mirror directory is un-ignored, not one skill at a time. Allowlisting
# each skill by name meant a newly mirrored skill was silently untracked: `git add -A`
# skipped it without error and every local check passed, because the file was on disk.
# It took a CI run on a fresh checkout to notice. That is the failure mode this repo
# refuses to fix with a reminder.
#
# What this un-ignoring would otherwise risk — sweeping a contributor's project-local
# scratch skill into a commit — is covered by a mechanism rather than by scoping:
# scripts/verify-mirror.sh rejects EVERY file under this directory that has no
# counterpart under plugins/quick-dev/skills/ — recursively, not just SKILL.md and
# references/* — and also any mirrored file git is not tracking.
!.claude/skills/

# Python bytecode. The shipped script is only ever executed, never imported by the plugin —
# but verify-knowledge-py.sh imports it to drive the lock's release-race case, and CPython
# writes __pycache__/ next to the source when it does. Left untracked-but-unignored that
# artifact lands in the next `git add -A`, which is how a .pyc reached this repo once.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Local optimization scratch — session transcripts, context dumps and analysis notes
# produced while measuring a run. It is working material for one investigation, never a
# repo artifact, and `optimize/session-log.txt` is a RAW SESSION LOG: the same class of
# content `feedback-harvest` redacts before archiving, and the kind a pull-request body
# routinely promises it does not ship.
#
# Untracked-but-unignored is the dangerous state, not untracked. The next `git add -A`
# commits the whole directory without a word, exactly as it once committed a .pyc and
# once skipped a newly mirrored skill. Two entries above already exist because that
# happened; this one exists so it does not happen with a transcript.
optimize/

node_modules/
.DS_Store
*.log
.env
.env.local
